      "writtenOn": "2021-04-05T06:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why should this make a difference ?\n\nIf I\u0027m reading the code correctly :\n• TetheringTest is using a BroadcastInterceptingContext with setUseRegisteredHandlers(true) ⇒ calling sendBroadcast will synchronously post a runnable on the handler thread\n• TestConnectivityManager#sendDefaultNetworkCallbacks posts the callbacks on the handler thread stored in the NRI\n\nAs long as the handler used by the context and the callbacks is the same (which it looks to be though I didn\u0027t check very thoroughly), dispatching between sending the broadcast and the callbacks (or the other way around) should have no impact on what is seen in UpstreamNetworkMonitor#getCurrentPreferredUpstream. It shouldn\u0027t matter whether the callback message is enqueued when CONNECTIVITY_ACTION is processed, and as such, calling dispatchAll() after both sendDefaultNetworkCallbacks and sendDefaultNetworkBroadcasts have been called should be sufficient. This would let you simplify the code by removing the runnable, which certainly is pretty intrusive in that its usage requires callers to understand minutely the inner mechanisms of the test.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1128,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1129,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "55adc38fa499d6b4a6c314f973754d0ba575acbf",
