      "writtenOn": "2021-04-05T06:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what this might mean in this context. IIUC, what matters is what the thread processing CONNECTIVITY_ACTION sees when querying UpstreamNetworkMonitor.mNetworkMap through #getCurrentPreferredUpstream. If we consider only one event triggering a callback and a broadcast, either the callback has been processed when the map is queried, or not.\n\nWell strictly speaking in fact there are 2 accesses to the map in the function, but none of this matters because everything is processed on the same thread anyway.\n\nUltimately, because all of this is handled on the SM thread, either the callback is handled before the query, or it\u0027s handled after. So I don\u0027t understand what \"both\" may mean.",
